1
00:00:02,978 --> 00:00:47,994
You're Tops

2
00:00:47,994 --> 00:00:50,011
Is that you, Susan?

3
00:00:50,011 --> 00:00:51,660
It's me, Grandpa.

4
00:00:51,660 --> 00:00:52,992
Am I glad to see you!

5
00:00:52,992 --> 00:00:55,476
And am I glad to see you!

6
00:00:55,476 --> 00:00:58,148
I am also glad to be here.

7
00:00:58,148 --> 00:00:59,654
How are things?

8
00:00:59,654 --> 00:01:01,845
I have been talking to a group of salesmen

9
00:01:01,845 --> 00:01:03,019
since ten this morning,

10
00:01:03,019 --> 00:01:05,428
and I'm real exhausted.

11
00:01:05,428 --> 00:01:07,325
Well, you look good.

12
00:01:07,325 --> 00:01:08,220
What's Harry doing tonight?

13
00:01:08,220 --> 00:01:08,574
He and Michelle

14
00:01:08,574 --> 00:01:10,825
are visiting relatives in New Jersey today.

15
00:01:10,825 --> 00:01:12,722
The rest of our family went to the movies.

16
00:01:12,722 --> 00:01:15,191
So it's just you and me, Susan.

17
00:01:15,191 --> 00:01:17,367
It's nice to be alone with you, Grandpa.

18
00:01:17,367 --> 00:01:18,752
We don't get to see enough of each other.

19
00:01:18,752 --> 00:01:20,370
Oh, I feel the same way, Susan.

20
00:01:20,370 --> 00:01:22,425
I miss seeing you.

21
00:01:22,425 --> 00:01:23,780
But to tell the truth,

22
00:01:23,780 --> 00:01:24,721
next time

23
00:01:24,721 --> 00:01:26,234
I'd like to go into the city and meet you there,

24
00:01:26,234 --> 00:01:28,726
instead of you coming here.

25
00:01:28,726 --> 00:01:29,991
You don't need to do that, Grandpa.

26
00:01:29,991 --> 00:01:31,526
Yeah, I do.

27
00:01:31,526 --> 00:01:34,582
I need to get out more.

28
00:01:34,582 --> 00:01:36,223
Well, I mean

29
00:01:36,223 --> 00:01:37,782
there's a lot to do around the house,

30
00:01:37,782 --> 00:01:39,061
and I love being here with the family,

31
00:01:39,061 --> 00:01:39,611
you know,

32
00:01:39,611 --> 00:01:42,938
but I'm restless.

33
00:01:42,938 --> 00:01:44,451
Since I retired,

34
00:01:44,451 --> 00:01:46,679
I've got extra time on my hands.

35
00:01:46,679 --> 00:01:49,156
I understand, Grandpa.

36
00:01:49,156 --> 00:01:50,774
I think you do.

37
00:01:50,774 --> 00:01:52,047
Frankly,

38
00:01:52,047 --> 00:01:54,553
I'd like to use my brain a little more.

39
00:01:54,553 --> 00:01:55,502
Grandpa,

40
00:01:55,502 --> 00:01:58,934
you have so much energy and so many years of experience.

41
00:01:58,934 --> 00:02:01,291
There are probably a lot of places for you to work

42
00:02:01,291 --> 00:02:03,564
Particularly in the construction field.

43
00:02:03,564 --> 00:02:05,100
But at my age,

44
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:07,079
I'm not looking for a full-time job.

45
00:02:07,079 --> 00:02:09,436
I'm retired.

46
00:02:09,436 --> 00:02:10,444
But I'm bored.

47
00:02:10,444 --> 00:02:14,690
Well, there must be something.

48
00:02:14,690 --> 00:02:17,934
Maybe I can help.

49
00:02:17,934 --> 00:02:19,417
Let's go into the kitchen,

50
00:02:19,417 --> 00:02:21,999
and maybe you can help me set the table.

51
00:02:21,999 --> 00:02:23,083
Sounds good to me.

52
00:02:23,083 --> 00:02:23,934
What are we having?

53
00:02:23,934 --> 00:02:25,590
I prepared lamb chops,

54
00:02:25,590 --> 00:02:28,044
mashed potatoes, and a tossed green salad to begin with.

55
00:02:28,044 --> 00:02:38,086
Grandpa, you are a terrific guy!

56
00:02:38,086 --> 00:02:40,096
You're still thinking about something to do, aren't you?

57
00:02:40,096 --> 00:02:41,150
A job of some kind.

58
00:02:41,150 --> 00:02:42,618
That's right.

59
00:02:42,618 --> 00:02:45,787
I've been thinking about it for weeks now.

60
00:02:45,787 --> 00:02:49,543
There must be some way to put my mind to good use.

61
00:02:49,543 --> 00:02:50,695
We'll find a solution.

62
00:02:50,695 --> 00:02:51,824
A positive solution

63
00:02:51,824 --> 00:02:51,824
to your finding a way to use that wonderful mind of yours.
